from e import *
E(6,'national-war-memorial','National War Memorial',
 ('A flame that never sleeps','Standing in the heart of the capital is a place where a flame burns day and night to remember brave people. This short poem takes you to that place, the National War Memorial in New Delhi.'),
 [('The memorial',['The National War Memorial in New Delhi was established in February 2019. It is a national monument built by the Government of India in honour of our brave soldiers.','The pictures show the memorial itself and Amar Jawan Jyoti, the eternal flame.']),
  ('What the poem says',['The poem describes the memorial as a grand sight in the heartland of Bharat, honouring brave stories that are told again and again.','It stands with respect, grace and pride, and every name and stone carries a story. The soldiers are remembered from battlefields, skies and wide oceans, because they stood for Bharat side by side.','The eternal flame glows in silence and pays homage to their courage. Their sacrifice is always in our minds, in blessed memory.','The poem ends with a promise to remember with pride and respect the sacrifice of the soldiers at the memorial.']),
  ('Activities',['Read the poem aloud, recite it with your classmates and teacher, and try to remember it.','Visit the website of the National War Memorial, given in the book as mygov.in, to learn more about it, and plan a visit with your teacher or parents.']),
  ('Listening passage and extra note',['This chapter\'s last page also holds the transcript for a listening task from Unit 5 about a dish called gakkad bharta, which a speaker from Jabalpur in Madhya Pradesh describes.','Gakkad is made from wheat dough balls roasted on high heat. Bharta is made by roasting brinjals and tomatoes and garnishing with chopped onions, coriander, green chillies and salt. It is made without frying, and is eaten by crumbling gakkad, adding bharta and a spoonful of ghee.'])],
 [('Say in one line what the eternal flame stands for in the poem.',[('Find the lines about the flame.','It glows in silence and pays homage to courage.'),('Link it to the soldiers.','It reminds us of their sacrifice, which we should always remember.')])],
 ('Explain what the National War Memorial is and what the poem says about it.',['It was established in February 2019 in New Delhi.','It honours brave soldiers.','The poem mentions battlefields, skies and oceans, the eternal flame, and remembering their sacrifice.'],['It was built in 1947.','It honours only sailors.']),
 ['The National War Memorial in New Delhi was established in February 2019.','It honours our brave soldiers, and Amar Jawan Jyoti is the eternal flame there.','The poem asks us to remember their sacrifice with pride and respect.','Read and recite the poem and visit the memorial website with your teacher.'],
 [('m','When was the National War Memorial established?','February 2019',[('August 1947','That is Independence, not the memorial.'),('January 1950','That is the date the Constitution came into effect.')],'The text says it was established in February 2019.'),
  ('m','Whom does the memorial honour?','Brave soldiers',[('Teachers','The memorial honours soldiers.'),('Farmers','The poem is about soldiers.')],'It was built in honour of our brave soldiers.'),
  ('t','The eternal flame glows in silence in the poem.',True,'It pays homage to the soldiers\' courage.'),
  ('m','What does Amar Jawan Jyoti refer to in the chapter?','The eternal flame',[('A school','It is shown in a picture of the memorial.'),('A river','The picture shows a flame.')],'Amar Jawan Jyoti is the flame of the memorial.'),
  ('m','From where do the soldiers in the poem stand for Bharat?','Battle fields, skies and oceans wide',[('Only the mountains','The poem lists three places, battlefields, skies and oceans.'),('Only the border towns','These are not named.')],'The poem lists battlefields, skies and oceans.'),
  ('t','The Government of India built the memorial.',True,'The text says it is a national monument built by the Government of India.'),
  ('m','How is gakkad cooked in the listening passage?','Roasted dough balls',[('Deep fried','The dish is made without frying.'),('Boiled in water','Dough balls are roasted on high heat.')],'The speaker from Jabalpur roasts wheat dough balls.'),
  ('m','What should we do after reading the poem?','Recite it and remember it',[('Rewrite it in prose','The activity says to recite and remember.'),('Ignore it','The chapter asks for reading aloud.')],'The activities ask us to read it aloud, recite it and remember it.'),
  ('s','Which city is the National War Memorial in?',['new delhi','New Delhi','delhi','Delhi'],'It is in New Delhi.'),
  ('s','In which month and year was it established?',['february 2019','February 2019','feb 2019'],'It was established in February 2019.')],
 keep=['memorial','eternal flame'])
